# Wave I.5 — Neutral wizard plugin load / resolve

## Problem

After I.4, `wizard/denali/` no longer imports product packages, but the **shell still speaks Denali** for the universal plugin load path:

| Symbol | File |
| ------ | ---- |
| `resolveDenaliSyncWorkspacePlugin` | `wizard/denali/resolve-sync-workspace-plugin.ts` |
| `loadDenaliWorkspacePlugin` | same |

Create + flat-edit call these as if only Denali exists. The implementation already delegates to draft-shell / `loadWorkspacePluginByIdFromRegistry` — the Denali brand is false coupling.

## Decision

1. Move module to [`apps/web/src/wizard/resolve-wizard-workspace-plugin.ts`](../../apps/web/src/wizard/resolve-wizard-workspace-plugin.ts) (out of the denali firewall folder).
2. Rename:

| Before | After |
| ------ | ----- |
| `resolveDenaliSyncWorkspacePlugin` | `resolveWizardSyncWorkspacePlugin` |
| `loadDenaliWorkspacePlugin` | `loadWizardWorkspacePlugin(pluginId?)` |

3. `loadWizardWorkspacePlugin` defaults `pluginId` to `DENALI_PLUGIN_ID` until create/edit pass session `pluginId` — **done in** [`wave-i-6-session-plugin-load.mdoc`](./wave-i-6-session-plugin-load.mdoc). Sync resolve still uses draft-shell Denali getter (generated) until multi-workspace draft-shell exists.
4. Update create/flat-edit call sites + boundary specs; **delete** `wizard/denali/resolve-sync-workspace-plugin.ts`.

## Out of scope

- Renaming `getDenaliWorkspacePluginFromDraftShell` (codegen)
- Passing session `pluginId` into every load site → **Wave I.6**; create still used sync Denali until **Wave I.9**
- Removing denali from `package.json` → first peel [`wave-i-7-host-install-classification.mdoc`](./wave-i-7-host-install-classification.mdoc)


## Status

**DONE** — module + renames landed; `wizard/denali/` is adapters + `workspace-plugin-id` only.

## Verify

```bash
rg 'loadDenaliWorkspacePlugin|resolveDenaliSyncWorkspacePlugin|resolve-sync-workspace-plugin' \
  apps/web --glob '!**/*.generated.*'
# expect empty in apps/web src/app (tests may assert absence)
pnpm run wave-i0:guard
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-i-5-wizard-plugin-load.spec.ts \
  test/workspace-boundary.spec.ts \
  test/p2-d4-flat-edit-io.spec.ts \
  test/wave-h-denali-wizard-adapters.spec.ts
```
